    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Cal Raleigh** stands as our premier play with a 77.68 score, buoyed by an elite +19% SP skill boost against Sugano. The matchup is prime for power, and his spot in the cleanup hole provides the necessary RBI leverage to anchor our lineup. Following closely, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (66.56) remains a must-start; while the SP skill modifier is slightly negative, his ability to capitalize on Perkins\u2019 slow delivery\u2014creating a stolen base opportunity\u2014keeps his ceiling high. In the outfield, **JJ Bleday** and **Bryce Harper** provide strong 65+ scores, with **JJ Bleday** benefiting from a robust +14% platoon edge against Peterson, and **Bryce Harper** continuing to demonstrate elite xwOBA metrics despite the park factor drag in his matchup against Tong.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Jung Hoo Lee** on the bench. His projection of 39.91 fell just fractions of a point below our 40.0 floor, effectively disqualifying him as we prioritize game cap preservation. While his spot batting 2nd and potential for stolen bases against Dreyer were appealing, the -19% SP skill penalty and a negative platoon split created a risk profile we couldn't justify for today\u2019s allocation. Elsewhere, we are navigating extreme difficulty against elite arms; **Zack Gelof**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, and **Dylan Beavers** all face the daunting task of overcoming Misiorowski or Williams, both of whom carry sub-3.00 xERAs. These players are currently starting, but their efficiency remains tethered to the assumption that they can manufacture runs despite the negative SP skill modifiers. We will keep a close eye on **Braden Montgomery**, whose 44.68 score is the lowest of our starters, as he remains the primary pivot if we need to pinch-hit for higher efficiency late in the day.",
